{"name":"Cauliflower","hex":"#ebe5d0","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"cauliflower","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Brassica oleracea var. botrytis, an annual variety of cabbage, of which the cluster of young flower stalks and buds is eaten as a vegetable.","The edible head or curd of a cauliflower plant."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To (cause to) swell up like a cauliflower ear."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cauliflower"}],"entries":[{"title":"Cauliflower","blocks":[{"text":"Cauliflower is a vegetable belonging to the species Brassica oleracea in the family Brassicaceae. It is one of several cultivated forms of the species along with cabbage, broccoli, Brussels sprouts, kale, kohlrabi, and others. The edible portion of the plant is its dense head of undeveloped flower buds known as the \"curd\". The head is usually white but may also be green, orange, or purple. Several cultivars exist, including the Romanesco variety, whose spiral curds grow in fractal patterns."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2f/Chou-fleur_02.jpg/330px-Chou-fleur_02.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cauliflower"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/df/Cauliflower_plants_growing_in_New_Jersey_in_April.jpg/500px-Cauliflower_plants_growing_in_New_Jersey_in_April.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/df/Cauliflower_plants_growing_in_New_Jersey_in_April.jpg/500px-Cauliflower_plants_growing_in_New_Jersey_in_April.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Cauliflower plants growing in a nursery","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACauliflower_plants_growing_in_New_Jersey_in_April.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/e/e1